# ==============================================================================
# .dockerignore — DocXReports API
#
# Excludes files from the Docker build context (what gets sent to the Docker
# daemon when you run "docker build").
#
# WHY this matters:
#   Docker sends the entire build context folder to the daemon before building.
#   Without this file, it would send node_modules, bin/obj folders, the entire
#   UMSReportsAPI project, .git history, temp files — potentially gigabytes
#   of data that the Dockerfile never needs. This file keeps the context small
#   and the build fast.
# ==============================================================================


# ── Build output — never needed, regenerated during build ────────────────────
**/bin/
**/obj/

# ── Visual Studio / IDE files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.vs/
**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/*.userosscache
**/*.sln.docstates
.vscode/
.idea/

# ── Git — we create a fresh dummy repo inside the container ──────────────────
# The real .git folder is excluded for two reasons:
#   1. It can be 100MB+ with full commit history
#   2. We create a clean throwaway git repo inside the build stage anyway
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ── UMSReportsAPI — the .NET Framework project, not needed for DocXReports ───
# This is the Crystal Reports / IIS project. It has nothing to do with the
# DocXReports Linux container. Excluding it keeps the build context small.
UMSReportsAPI/

# ── Windows Dockerfile — not needed inside the Linux image build ──────────────
Dockerfile.windows

# ── Docker Compose — not needed inside the image ─────────────────────────────
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose*.yml

# ── Temp and lock files left by LibreOffice / Windows ────────────────────────
**/*.tmp
**/*.temp
**/~$*
**/DocXHtmlToPdfConverterTmp/

# ── Already-rendered output — these are runtime artifacts, not source files ──
DocXReports/Resources/

# ── NuGet package cache — packages are restored fresh during build ────────────
# If you have a local packages/ folder, exclude it — NuGet restores from
# nuget.org inside the container anyway.
packages/
*.nupkg

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/*.log
**/logs/

# ── Misc project files not needed in the image ───────────────────────────────
clip.txt
*.7z
*.zip
*.rar
README*
CHANGELOG*
*.md

# ── DocxTemplater test / markdown projects — only core library is needed ──────
DocxTemplater-main/DocxTemplater.Test/
DocxTemplater-main/DocxTemplater.Markdown/
DocxTemplater-main/**/*.md
DocxTemplater-main/**/*.txt
DocxTemplater-main/**/.git/
